{# Runtime half of the token layer.

   `aropixel_admin.theme.colors` is a PHP-level theming API that predates the CSS tokens.
   It used to be applied as inline `style=` attributes, and an inline style beats tokens,
   the Bootstrap bridge, cascade layers and `!important` alike — so an install themed
   through the config could not be restyled through the documented CSS API at all. Two
   theming systems, one silently outranking the other.

   Emitting it as custom properties folds the PHP API into the CSS one: the config still
   wins, but it wins *as a token*, which every component already reads.

   Must be included after the stylesheet links so it overrides the static defaults in
   css/foundations/_tokens.css. Values come from application configuration, not user
   input. #}
<style>
    :root {
        --aro-color-primary: {{ admin_theme.colors.btn_background_color }};
        --aro-color-primary-contrast: {{ admin_theme.colors.btn_color }};
        --aro-login-side-bg: {{ admin_theme.colors.background_color }};
    }
</style>
